          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "મંગાવવું — mangāvvũ — \"to order, to send for\"."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "અમે હોટેલમાંથી ચા મંગાવીએ છીએ. — ame hoṭelmā̃thī cā mangāvīe chīe — \"We order tea from the hotel.\""
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "માગવું asks for a thing; મંગાવવું (mangāvvũ) has it brought."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 2,
          "type": "etymology",
          "title": "The word, taken apart",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "મંગાવવું (mangāvvũ) is built on māgvũ, \"to ask for\", with the causative ending -āvvũ: \"to have something brought\". māgvũ is a tadbhava from Sanskrit mā́rgati, \"seeks, requests\" (CDIAL 10074)."
            }
          ]
        },
